<title>BELGIUM: Distrigas group profit falls five pct.</title>
<headline>Distrigas group profit falls five pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		 1,206	   vs  1,270</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		  1,299	   vs  1,402</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		   66,380	   vs 56,636</p>
<p>    Dividend (francs)		  945	   vs    900</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 3,551	   vs  3,677</p>
<p>    Financial loss		   1,122	   vs  1,192</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charges	    200	   vs     72</p>
<p>    Taxes				  930	   vs  1,011</p>
<p>    Total investments		1,575	   vs  1,285</p>
<p>Dividend payment date May 28, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Gas pipeline operator Distrigas said natural gas sales rose by 11 percent for the second succesive year due mainly to the cold weather. It said total volume that passed through the Belgian grid was 16.7 billion cubic metres, up from 13 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
